![](/media/2018/04/IMG20180401174655.jpg) The house in Conakry, Guinea where I stayed. We took all of our classes from the house and every morning we watched the fisherman out at sea. ![](/media/2018/04/IMG20180330173804.jpg) The view from our balcony out onto the streets of Kaporo, Conakry. ![](/media/2018/04/IMG20180330085633.jpg) First Dundunba with Merveille Ballet. The dancing and drumming was phenomenal!   ![](/media/2018/04/IMG20180330085452.jpg) Merveille Ballet Dundunba ![](/media/2018/04/IMG20180325214037.jpg) A baby ceremony that we attended on day 2. Still jetlagged and wide eyed from all of the fabulous fabric that the women wear. Here we saw goats being sacrificed and the drummers that played for our dance classes played Dundunba and Soko. ![](/media/2018/04/IMG20180325212932.jpg) The kids were always fascinated and happy to be a part of the photos. ![](/media/2018/04/IMG20180325210758.jpg) Baby Ceremony. ![](/media/2018/04/IMG20180325210751.jpg) Baby Ceremony. ![](/media/2018/04/IMG_2929.jpg) Djembe lesson with legend FAMOUDOU KONATE. ![](/media/2018/04/IMG_2925.jpg) Dance class with Buntu from Merveille Ballet. ![](/media/2018/04/IMG_2922.jpg) Drummers from Merveille Ballet,  drumming for our dance classes. ![](/media/2018/04/IMG_2918.jpg) Learning amazing choreography, dripping with sweat and always smiling! ![](/media/2018/04/IMG_2912.jpg) Buntu our dance teacher.
